WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.800
Virtual appliances, vNIOS,
run on VMware, Azure and AWS.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.354
On VMware, the advice is to
leave the VM's settings alone,

3
00:00:09.354 --> 00:00:14.250
because changing them may violate the
licensing terms and stop it joining.

4
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:20.607
On Azure and AWS, high availability arrived
in 9.0.4, with limits to plan around,

5
00:00:20.607 --> 00:00:26.863
such as both nodes in the same region
and zone, and no IPv6 failover.

6
00:00:26.863 --> 00:00:30.688
The HA prerequisites list the
commercial cloud endpoints,

7
00:00:30.688 --> 00:00:33.420
which is where the
program's workloads run,

8
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:37.713
and failover time depends on each
cloud's API, so test it in the pilot.

9
00:00:37.713 --> 00:00:43.490
And one constraint that shapes Part 2: vNIOS
members can't manage Microsoft servers.
